# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
# Display configuration fragment for Xiaomi Pad 5 (nabu)
# The SM8150 DPU/DSI stack is built in; the NT36523 panel and the KTZ8866
# backlight are modules, matching the known-good senemos 7.2.2 bring-up.  With
# the panel built in it probes during the very first DSI power-on while the
# controller still holds the bootloader's video-mode state; as a module it
# probes later, after the display core has settled.
CONFIG_DRM_MSM=y
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_NOVATEK_NT36523=y
CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_KTZ8866=y

# Linux 7.2 gpiolib-shared auto-scans every *-gpios property and shares it
# with remoteproc ("gpiolib_shared.proxy") consumers.  On nabu this captures
# the panel "reset-gpios" (<&tlmm 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>); the pin then ends up
# driven low (reset asserted) instead of high, so the NT36523 panel never
# comes out of reset and the screen stays black.  6.14 has no such automatic
# sharing and drives the line directly.  Disable it so the panel driver owns
# the reset line as before.
# CONFIG_GPIO_SHARED is not set
# CONFIG_GPIO_SHARED_PROXY is not set
